sh the saved P3a VI"}},{"tool_name":"PowerShell","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KvWTmNCB8zDoJvY7yAovTZ","tool_input":{"command":"Get-FileHash -Algorithm MD5 -LiteralPath \"C:\\Program Files\\National Instruments\\LabVIEW 2026\\user.lib\\claudeDev\\D1_ring_p2b_20261001_140658.vi\"","timeout":30000,"description":"Hash the P2b bed to confirm unchanged"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SNGyzm3Y6evjHVXUtNvL2V","tool_input":{"command":"py tools/protocol.py validate tools/bench/next.json; py tools/protocol.py validate tools/bench/cards/result_124-8.json; wc -l STATUS.md; py tools/retro_due.py --cycle 124; echo rc=$?","timeout":30000,"description":"Validate next.json, STATUS length, retrospective due check"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":8,"requested":{"background":3,"foreground":5,"unset":0},"started_in_background":3,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":8,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"material":8}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":113,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Cycle 124 delivered ring step P3a, the next saved VI of the ring buffer; the cycle is closed.\n\n**New working VI:** `claudeDev\\D1_ring_p3a_20261001_180540.vi` (md5 `4dfa44aa…`). It adds the control part of loop 1.1:\n- a 1 ms wait;\n- a register holding the previous buffer number, starting at −1;\n- an `Equal?` comparison feeding a case: True means a duplicate frame, False a new frame;\n- a new-frame counter (starting at 0, raised only for new frames) and slot index `i = count mod 20`.\n\n**How it was built:** the scratch run and the one real build both passed 22/0, and the object counts matched the prediction. The Error List has 55 items: the 54 from P2b plus one new \"Wire has loose ends\". That is the alternative count the plan predicted, and the expected-list file checks OK. It is structural only: it compiles but is broken by design and has never been run. Broken-file count is now 2 of 6. STATUS.md now points to it as the working VI.\n\n**New tools:**\n- An op VI, `claudeDev\\OpConnectTermUid_v0.vi`, that wires any terminal to any terminal by ID. It passed the 2,000-call check with the handle count flat.\n- On top of it, scratch functions for case tunnels: `connect_term_uid`, `case_inner_face` and `case_frame_wire`. They also reach a shift register's inner terminal across a case border, which no earlier function could. The P4 step needs this too.\n- The plan format and simulator now accept a `frame` field for wires that end inside a case frame.\n\n**Card failures along the way:**\n- Two were bugs in our own build script; both fixed.\n- One build card's real problem turned out to be the shift-register crossing, not the case frame. The new op closed it.\n- One stopped because the plan left the terminal class unset on new nodes. The plan now copies measured classes.\n- One offline card was wrongly refused by a gate; this and three other gate false alarms (fp-10 to fp-13) wait in the queue for the next batch fix.\n\n**Next cycle's first act:**\n1. Find which wire the 55th Error List item points to, and whether P3b is expected to consume it.\n2. Make the pre-run check refuse any new node whose terminal classes are not declared.\n3. Build the Flat Sequence creator (a new op with its 2,000-call check).\n4. Then P3b, the slot writes.\n\n`next.json` and STATUS NEXT are written. The runner continues; nothing is blocked.\n\n**Decision for you:** D-2026-10-01-01 is still open. It sets P3b's size: either keep the 6-file limit on broken intermediate VIs and allow about 40 rows per build step, each with a full scratch run first (recommended), or keep the 15–25-row limit and spend more of the six files. If it is still unanswered when P3b is ready, P3b goes ahead under the recommended option.\n\nSTATUS.md is at 105 lines, just over the ~100-line limit. The next cycle should move the older cycle notes into the archive.\n\nThe Figma connector needs authorising in your claude.ai connector settings; it was not needed this cycle.","ttft_ms":2150,"type":"result","duration_ms":8723673,"uuid":"0612142e-4398-4eed-95fb-fb3795d6f4fc","ttft_stream_ms":1833,"time_to_request_ms":225,"first_content_frame_ms":1833,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
